 rate is $0.5$ ounces per dollar. Therefore, Rohan can buy $0.5$ ounces of specialty cheese for $1$ dollar." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514418 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186514260 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514418 #edb/ref 1069 "q-68919" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514418 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514418 #edb/ref 1071 "At Joe's market, the unit price of tomatoes is $$5$ per pound. How many pounds of tomatoes can Geena buy for $$1?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514418 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6ad6d7d2-b42a-533b-a893-138de3271ac7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514418 #edb/ref 1074 "We are given the unit rate of $$5$ per pound (dollars per pound). To find how many pounds of tomatoes she can buy for  $$1,$ we need to find the unit rate in pounds per dollar. So, we take the reciprocal: \n\n$$\n5\\,\\text{dollars per pound}\\,\\to \\,1÷5=0.2\\,\\text{pounds per dollar}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $0.2$ pounds per dollar. Therefore, Geena can buy $0.2$ pounds of tomatoes for $1$ dollar." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514453 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186514253 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514453 #edb/ref 1069 "q-91913" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514453 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514453 #edb/ref 1071 "In a snack store, there are three different types of cookies that come in boxes: \n\n- Box $A$ contains $13$ pounds, and costs $$3.77\\,.$\n\n- Box $B$ contains $10.5$ pounds, and costs $$3.15\\,.$\n\n- Box $C$ contains $12$ pounds, and costs $$3.48\\,.$\n\nWhich box of cookies is the best deal?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514453 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b32ba521-b62e-5f22-bb06-26d27c73470d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514453 #edb/ref 1074 "The best deal is the one with the lowest unit price. So, we need to compute the unit prices for all three boxes. To compute the unit price, we divide the cost by the total number of pounds.  \n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of pounds in box $A$,  we get\n\n$$\n3.77÷13=0.29\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of box $A$ is $$0.29$  per pound.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of pounds in box $B$,  we get\n\n$$\n3.15÷10.5=0.30\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bag $B$ is $$0.30$  per pound.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of pounds in box $C$,  we get\n\n$$\n3.48÷12=0.29\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of box $C$ is $$0.29$  per pound.\n\nFrom the above, we see that boxes $A$ and $C$ have the lowest unit price. Therefore, boxes $A$ and $C$ are the best deals." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514462 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186514274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514462 #edb/ref 1069 "q-68863" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514462 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514462 #edb/ref 1071 "Jack bought a pumpkin that weighed $3$ kilograms. The retail price of pumpkin at the store is  $$1.78/kg.$ How much did  Jack pay for the pumpkin?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514462 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c993b31b-1739-52ac-a2f5-55deea55eaf7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514462 #edb/ref 1074 "The unit price of pumpkin is $$1.78/kg.$ To find the cost of  $3$ kilograms of pumpkin, we multiply:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1.78\\times 3 & =5.34\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Jack paid  $$5.34$ for the $3$-$\\text{kg}$ pumpkin." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514481 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186514266 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514481 #edb/ref 1069 "q-68901" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514481 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514481 #edb/ref 1071 "Lucy's Treats sells three different boxes of raisins: \n\n- Box $A$ contains $12$ ounces, and costs $$2.28\\,.$\n\n- Box $B$ contains $32$ ounces,  and costs $$5.44\\,.$\n\n- Box $C$ contains $22$ ounces, and costs $$3.52\\,.$\n\nWhich box of raisins is the best deal?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514481 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fa60ae23-8081-566e-ab07-1797ceb80d43" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514481 #edb/ref 1074 "The best deal is the box with the lowest unit price. So, we need to compute the unit prices for all three boxes. To compute the unit price, we divide the price by the total number of ounces.   \n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in box $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n2.28÷12=0.19\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of box $A$ is $$0.19.$\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in box $B,$ we get\n\n$$\n5.44÷32=0.17\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of box $B$ is $$0.17.$\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in box $C,$ we get\n\n$$\n3.52÷22=0.16\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of box $C$ is $$0.16.$\n\nFrom the above, we see that box $C$ has the lowest unit price of $$0.16/\\text{oz}.$ Therefore, box $C$ offers the best deal." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514507 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186514521 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514507 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6808d3f3-1bd6-54f5-b886-4da1e7511ffe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514507 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186514453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514510 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186514507 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514510 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "75590325-0b56-5c97-a717-ef93b875f262" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514510 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186514418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514521 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a6853681-9bf8-57e0-aa5a-d730ef04cfc0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514521 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186514380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514525 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186514510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514525 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b67b97a8-1d26-577a-b9f1-8e74866dde08" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514525 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186514481 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514548 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186514525 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514548 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fcb274d6-4201-5c3e-bf1f-dac0c